1️⃣ Raspberry Pi Access Point Configuration

Purpose

The Raspberry Pi functions as:

· Access Point (WiFi Venue)
· MQTT Broker
· Backend Server
· Frontend Server

Thus, the entire system can operate without internet.

Topology:

```text
Operator Laptop
       │
       │ WiFi
       ▼
 Raspberry Pi (Access Point)
       │
       ├── Frontend
       ├── Backend API
       ├── MQTT Broker
       │
       ▼
 ESP32 
       │
       ▼
      LoRa
       │
       ▼
  Arduino Mega Display
```

---

Install Access Point Packages

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y

sudo apt install hostapd dnsmasq -y
```

Enable service:

```bash
sudo systemctl unmask hostapd
sudo systemctl enable hostapd
```

---

Set Static IP for WLAN

Edit:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/dhcpcd.conf
```

Add:

```text
interface wlan0
static ip_address=192.168.50.1/24
nohook wpa_supplicant
```

Restart:

```bash
sudo service dhcpcd restart
```

---

DHCP Server Configuration

Backup configuration:

```bash
sudo mv /etc/dnsmasq.conf /etc/dnsmasq.conf.backup
```

Create new configuration:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/dnsmasq.conf
```

Content:

```text
interface=wlan0
dhcp-range=192.168.50.10,192.168.50.100,255.255.255.0,24h
```

---

Hostapd Configuration

```bash
sudo nano /etc/hostapd/hostapd.conf
```

Content:

```text
country_code=ID

interface=wlan0
driver=nl80211

ssid=VENUE-SCOREBOARD

hw_mode=g
channel=6

wmm_enabled=0

auth_algs=1

ignore_broadcast_ssid=0

wpa=2
wpa_passphrase=Venue12345

wpa_key_mgmt=WPA-PSK
rsn_pairwise=CCMP
```

---

Connect Hostapd

Edit:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/default/hostapd
```

Change to:

```text
DAEMON_CONF="/etc/hostapd/hostapd.conf"
```

---

Run Access Point

```bash
sudo systemctl restart hostapd
sudo systemctl restart dnsmasq
```

Verification:

```bash
sudo systemctl status hostapd
```

---

Reboot

```bash
sudo reboot
```

---

Verification

SSID:

```text
VENUE-SCOREBOARD
```

Password:

```text
